{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data warehouse data warehouse","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","fileName":"Data Warehouse.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Warehouse","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-09 03:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Mining Process and Infrastructure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Mining Process and Infrastructure","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data warehouse data warehouse","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","fileName":"Data Warehouse.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Warehouse","heading":"Data Warehouse","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A data warehouse is a subject-oriented, integrated, time-varying, and generally non-updatable collection designed to support management decisions and business intelligence. It consolidates data from otherwise separate operational sources.\n\nA common, high-quality repository gives data mining a consistent view of organizational history. It does not remove the need to understand provenance, definitions, or changes in source systems.\n\nThe book adds that a warehouse can materially shorten individual data science projects because extraction, standardization, and integration have already been done for shared use. Its historic records also allow models to be rolled through earlier time periods and checked for changing accuracy. A central repository is helpful, not a prerequisite for data science.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Mining Process and Infrastructure","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data warehouse data warehouse","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Warehouse.md","fileName":"Data Warehouse.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Warehouse","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf]]\n\n[[datascience_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Mining Process and Infrastructure","clusteranalysisanddatamining.pdf","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}